\date{}
\begin{document}
\maketitle
\section{Introduction}
Hukumina (ISO 639-3 huw) was an Austronesian language of northwest Buru, Maluku, Indonesia. Search results indicate it is extinct, with one speaker recorded in 1989. Very little documentation exists.
\section{Primary Educational Resources}
None found.
\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Wikipedia, Hukumina language: \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hukumina_language}
\item Wikipedia, Palumata language (closely related, unattested): \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palumata_language}
\item ASJP word-list entry for Hukumina: \url{https://asjp.clld.org/languages/HUKUMINA}
\item Digging for the Roots of Language Death in Eastern Indonesia: The Cases of Kayeli and Hukumina (ANU repository): \url{https://openresearch-repository.anu.edu.au/handle/1885/39691?mode=full}
\item Endangered Languages of Austronesia (OUP chapter on the topic): \url{https://academic.oup.com/book/27194/chapter/196640810}
\end{itemize}
\section{Religious and Community Resources}
None found.
\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
None found.
\section{Curriculum Development Context}
With no known speakers and only a short word list and a sociolinguistic study, a language-medium curriculum is not feasible. A heritage curriculum could cover the history of the Hukumina people and the Buru language ecology, using the sources above, ideally with Buru community input.
\end{document}
